+
+## Voyage 2 — Editing empty-delete browser safety
+
+**Defect:** External browser acceptance suite reports `NotFoundError: Failed to execute 'removeChild' on 'Node'` when deleting a todo via empty edit. The `focusout` handler calls `saveEdit(li)` after the `keydown` handler has already removed the `<li>` from the DOM via `removeTodo` → `render()`. In happy-dom the second call is skipped (detached `closest` returns null); in a real browser the async `focusout` fires after the keydown handler returns and `closest` traverses the detached tree successfully.
+
+**Root cause:** `saveEdit` in `js/app.js` has no guard against operating on a detached `<li>`. The `focusout` handler at line ~270 unconditionally calls `saveEdit(li)` when the `<li>` has class `editing`, without checking whether the node is still in the DOM.
+
+**Specs written:** `features/editing-empty-safety.feature` (product behaviour), `features/editing-conformance.feature` (source-level guard check).
+
+**Watchbill:** `watchbill.json` with two watches targeting the new scenarios.
+
+**Next:** QM dispatch to implement the undefined steps and verify the scenarios go red on current code, then Crew to fix `saveEdit`.
